# Windows batch launchers must always be checked out with CRLF line endings.
# cmd.exe's batch parser can misparse REM comment lines and other statements
# when the file has LF-only endings, causing stray words to be executed as
# invalid commands (this broke start.bat's startup entirely). This rule keeps
# them CRLF on checkout regardless of any machine's core.autocrlf setting.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
